================================================================================
REVENUE CAP

This license is available to any individual or organization with total annual
revenue (ARR) of $1,000,000 USD or less.

This revenue cap applies to closed-source deployments of TPipe. If your
organization exceeds $1,000,000 USD in annual revenue, you must within
30 days either:

  (a) Enter a written Commercial Agreement with Ten Trillion Triangles LLC,
      or

  (b) Discontinue use of this license and switch to AGPL-3.0 by releasing
      your TPipe modifications under AGPL terms

Failure to convert within 30 days converts your license to AGPL-3.0
retroactively, back-dated to the date you exceeded $1,000,000 ARR.

Revenue is self-reported. Ten Trillion Triangles LLC reserves the right to
request annual revenue attestation. If you overstate your revenue to remain
under this cap, you owe 2x the applicable Commercial rate for every year of
non-compliance plus audit costs for an 18-month period following detection.

================================================================================
FOSS CARVE-OUT

If your project meets ALL of the following conditions, you are exempt from
the revenue cap above, and may use TPipe under these terms regardless of
your organization's revenue:

  (a) Your project's complete source code is publicly available under an
      OSI-approved license. The source code must be genuinely accessible —
      posting only a binary, a source archive without build instructions,
      or code behind a contribution agreement does not satisfy this
      requirement. Your project must be buildable from the publicly
      available source by a third party.

  (b) TPipe is used as a dependency, not distributed as a standalone
      product or under a different license name.

  (c) Your project does not itself compete with TPipe (see Noncompete).

Your FOSS project must still comply with the Noncompete clause. A FOSS project
that provides LLM orchestration or multi-agent pipeline functionality as a
competing product to others — regardless of whether the code is open — is not
eligible for this carve-out and must obtain a Commercial Agreement.

================================================================================
AUTOMATIC COMMERCIAL CONVERSION

If at any fiscal year end your ARR attributable to your TPipe-using product
or service exceeds $1,000,000 USD, you must transition to a Commercial
Agreement within 30 days of that date.

Transition options:
  - Contact Ten Trillion Triangles LLC to negotiate a Commercial Agreement
  - Discontinue this license and switch to AGPL-3.0

